        "@value": "For the uncovered tail (imaging/eCOA/DHT/genomics with no open identifier): the clinician/PI Attestation that certifies a binding at the catalog when it cannot be auto-resolved. Model the attestation path as first-class, not an exception (open Q6). E.g. imaging reviewed by the PI on receipt."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain": [
      {
        "@id": "https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#VendorAlias"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@value": "resolution attested by"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range": [
      {
        "@id": "https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#Attestation"
      }
    ],
    "https://top.scientix.ai/v1#flavor": [
      {
        "@value": "Additive"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#resolutionConfidence",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@value": "Confidence [0,1] of an automatic alias resolution. Below the threshold the binding is routed to the attestation queue, not auto-accepted."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@value": "resolution confidence"
